#!/usr/local/bin/python3.13 -I
"""contracts: contract radar: the owner's running contracts and recurring costs, from paperless cards only.

  contracts scan [--refresh] [--budget SECONDS] [--workers N] [--json]
        paperless metadata (`recent --json`) + one card per relevant document (`get ID --json`: date,
        correspondent, type, title, amount, currency, due date; cached 30 days) → contracts grouped by
        correspondent (else a known provider in the title, else the title's first word) and document type
        family; cadence guessed from the document dates (monthly / quarterly / half-yearly / yearly), last
        amount, yearly cost estimate, next expected bill. Read-only on paperless.
  contracts show [--all] [--json]   phone-sized card: top costs, total per year, "no bill for >1.5 cycles →
                                    maybe ended?", cancelled ones; --all lists every contract with its key
  contracts notice [--all] [--json] where a notice period matters: health insurance gets the KVG basic-insurance
                                    deadline (must ARRIVE by 30.11., last working day; kk-compare's deadline());
                                    everything else "notice period unknown — needs his ✅ per document", never
                                    guessed, unless he gave it (`set --notice`)
                                    Banks (accounts, status "account") and car hire (one-off) never get a notice entry.
  contracts ebill [--json]          (also `contracts --ebill`) recurring billers seen in paperless (documents, cadence,
                                    last bill) and whether each offers eBill / direct debit, from public payment-option
                                    pages (EBILL below); health uses kk-compare's insurer. LSV+/BDD end 30.09.2028.
  contracts warranty [WORD…] [--all] [--json] [--max N] [--budget S]   (also `contracts --warranty`)
        shop invoices and receipts (type Rechnung/Quittung/receipt/…, or such a word in the title) from a retailer
        or maker store (SHOPS below + his private "shop" entries) with "covered until" = invoice date + 24 months
        (the Swiss legal default, OR 210; shop/maker terms may give more or less: unverified), newest first, the
        title (without ids, dates, the shop's and his own name) as the item. Default: still covered; --all: all;
        WORD filters titles and shops (word prefixes) and then lists expired matches too. Live metadata
        (`recent --json`, falls back to the last scan's), amounts from cached cards; cards missing for these
        documents are fetched for up to --budget seconds (default 20; 0 = none) unless a scan holds the lock.
        Shop purchases are not contracts: scan/show skip them (a shop that is also a provider, e.g. Apple, stays).
  contracts set KEY [--name N] [--kind K] [--cadence C] [--ignore|--unignore] [--ended|--active]
                    [--notice TEXT] [--merge-into KEY2]
        owner corrections (KEY: a contract key from `show --all`, or a unique part of its name)

Privacy: cards only. Never `--content`, `--reason`, `fields`, `download` (those need the owner's ✅ in the vault
bot); titles are shown without digits, ids or the owner's own name. State (private, 0700/0600):
~/.local/state/contracts/ (cards.json: metadata + card cache; contracts.json: the last scan's result;
overrides.json: his corrections). No personal values in this file: provider names are public company names.
Env (tests): CONTRACTS_STATE_DIR, CONTRACTS_PAPERLESS (paperless command), CONTRACTS_NOW (YYYY-MM-DD),
CONTRACTS_KK (kk-compare path), CONTRACTS_KK_PROFILE (kk-compare profile), CONTRACTS_PROVIDERS (private extra providers), ASSISTANT_PROFILE. Tests: ~/opt/contracts-tests (test_contracts.py).
"""
